#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Analyse the failure history of a test using the Develocity API.

Given a test container (class/suite) and optionally a single test case, this
collects every execution of that test in a time window, groups the failures by
normalised failure message and stack trace, and reports where, when and how
often each distinct failure happened -- broken down by the tag combination
(branch / browser / database / servlet container) the test ran with.

Data sources (all reachable with the Develocity access key):
  * REST  GET /api/tests/cases        -> outcome per build scan id (1 request)
  * MCP   execute_query (DRV/Athena)  -> build attributes of all those scans in
                                         bulk (1 request per 900 scans)
  * MCP   get_build (failures)        -> message + stack trace of a failure
                                         (1 request per failing build, cached)

The build attributes also carry the URL of the Jenkins build that published the
scan, which is used to link the screenshot and the video that Jenkins archived
for the most recent occurrences of each failure (anonymous requests to
ci.xwiki.org, 1 per build, cached for a day since Jenkins discards the artifacts
of old builds).

Credentials are taken from $DEVELOCITY_URL / $DEVELOCITY_ACCESS_KEY or, failing
that, from the `Authorization: Bearer ...` extraHeader that the Develocity agent
skills repository leaves in ~/.gitconfig, or from the Develocity MCP server
configured for Claude Code (`mcpServers` in ~/.claude.json / $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR
or in a project `.mcp.json`).

With --recent-failures it works the other way round and lists the tests that
failed recently, marking each as a new or an already known failure, to find
candidates worth analysing.

Examples:
  dv-test-history 'org.xwiki.panels.test.ui.docker.AllIT$NestedNavigationPanelAdministrationIT#navigationPanelAdministration'
  dv-test-history --days 60 'https://community.develocity.cloud/scans/tests?...&tests.container=...&tests.test=...'
  dv-test-history --group-by stack --json out.json 'org.xwiki.foo.AllIT$NestedBarIT'
  dv-test-history --recent-failures 48
"""

